  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "b1.travel.lisbon-trip",
      "level": "B1",
      "topics": ["travel"],
      "title": "A trip to Lisbon",
      "text": "Last summer, my friends and I traveled to Lisbon. Although our flight was delayed for two hours, we arrived in time for dinner. We had booked a small room near the river. On the second day we got lost in the old town, but a friendly local showed us the way back. When I was a child, I used to think Portugal was very far away, but now it feels like a second home.",
      "source": {
        "kind": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b1.travel.backpacking-year",
      "level": "B1",
      "topics": ["travel"],
      "title": "A year with one backpack",
      "text": "My cousin Elena has traveled more than anyone I know. She has been to eleven countries, and she has never booked an expensive hotel. Last year she decided to go abroad for twelve months with only one backpack. She set off from Madrid in March. In the first week she missed a train in France because she was sleeping at the station, so she had to wait until the next morning. In Italy, the airline lost her luggage for three days. Although it was annoying, she bought a few cheap clothes and kept going. She spent most of her money on sightseeing, not on souvenirs. She checked in at small hostels, where she met other travelers and practiced her English every day. When she came home in February, she told us that the trip had changed her. Now she is planning her next adventure in South America. Have you ever traveled alone? Elena says everyone should try it at least once.",
      "source": {
        "kind": "original"
      }
    }
  ],
